### 3. Best Practices for Firebase Security

#### A. Firestore Security Rules
The most critical security practice is ensuring users can only access their own data. The rule should check that the `auth.uid` matches the `userId` of the document.

```javascript
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /users/{userId} {
      // Allow the user to read and write only their own profile document
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
    }
  }
}
```

#### B. Storage Rules
Ensure users can only upload profile pictures to their own specific folder in Firebase Storage.

```javascript
service firebase.storage {
  match /b/{bucket}/o {
    match /profiles/{userId}/{allPaths=**} {
      // Only the owner can upload/change their profile picture
      allow write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
      // Allow authenticated users to view profiles
      allow read: if request.auth != null;
    }
  }
}
```

